Run successfully.

---

# Step 6: Read Snowflake Table

```scala
val df = session.table("EMPLOYEE")
df.show()
```

Output:

```text
----------------------------------
|EMP_ID |EMP_NAME |SALARY|
----------------------------------
|1      |JOHN     |5000  |
|2      |SMITH    |6000  |
|3      |DAVID    |7000  |
----------------------------------
```

---

# Step 7: Filter Data

```scala
import com.snowflake.snowpark.functions._

val filteredDF =
  session.table("EMPLOYEE")
         .filter(col("SALARY") > 5500)

filteredDF.show()
```

Output:

```text
SMITH 6000
DAVID 7000
```

---

# Step 8: Select Specific Columns

```scala
val selectedDF =
  session.table("EMPLOYEE")
         .select(col("EMP_NAME"))

selectedDF.show()
```

Output:

```text
JOHN
SMITH
DAVID
```

---

# Step 9: Add New Column

```scala
val bonusDF =
  session.table("EMPLOYEE")
         .withColumn(
            "BONUS",
            col("SALARY") * 0.10
          )

bonusDF.show()
```

Output:

```text
EMP_ID EMP_NAME SALARY BONUS
1      JOHN     5000   500
2      SMITH    6000   600
3      DAVID    7000   700
```

---

# Step 10: Aggregate Data

```scala
val aggDF =
  session.table("EMPLOYEE")
         .agg(sum(col("SALARY")))

aggDF.show()
```

Output:

```text
18000
```

---

# Step 11: Create New Snowflake Table

```scala
bonusDF.write.mode("overwrite").saveAsTable("EMPLOYEE_BONUS")
```

Verify in Snowflake:

```sql
SELECT * FROM EMPLOYEE_BONUS;
```

